"""English companion report and CSV exports for the portrait comparison."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,csv,shutil,sys
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];OUT=ROOT/'results/grip_comparison'
CYCLES='--full-cycle' in sys.argv;PHYSIOLOGY='--physiology' in sys.argv or CYCLES
CASES={g:OUT/f'grip_{g}'/('cycle' if CYCLES else '')/('physiology' if PHYSIOLOGY else '') for g in [65,80]}
panels=[('delt_front_force_N','Anterior deltoid'),('delt_middle_force_N','Middle deltoid'),('upper_pec_force_N','Clavicular pec'),('triceps_force_N','Triceps'),('biceps_force_N','Biceps'),('latissimus_force_N','Latissimus dorsi'),('rotator_cuff_force_N','Rotator cuff'),('shoulder_resultant_N','Shoulder reaction'),('elbow_resultant_N','Elbow reaction'),('wrist_resultant_N','Wrist reaction')]
reports={g:json.loads((CASES[g]/'grip_traces.json').read_text('utf-8')) for g in CASES}
for g in CASES:shutil.copyfile(CASES[g]/'grip_traces.csv',OUT/f'grip_{g}_traces.csv')
rows=[]
with (OUT/'grip_summary.csv').open('w',encoding='utf-8-sig',newline='') as f:
 writer=csv.writer(f);writer.writerow(['metric','unit','standard_mean','standard_peak','wide_mean','wide_peak'])
 for key,label in panels:
  div=1 if key=='latissimus_force_N' else 1000;unit='N' if div==1 else 'kN'
  a,b=[reports[g]['summaries'][key] for g in [65,80]];values=[a['mean_ascent']/div,a['max_ascent']/div,b['mean_ascent']/div,b['max_ascent']/div]
  writer.writerow([label,unit,*values]);rows.append(f'<tr><td>{label}</td><td>{unit}</td>'+''.join(f'<td>{v:.3f}</td>' for v in values)+'</tr>')
cycle_text='''<h2>Three complete cycles</h2><p>Each cycle contains 2.0 s ascent, 0.3 s top hold, 2.0 s descent and 0.3 s bottom hold. The same 4.6 s cycle is replayed three times; fatigue and between-repetition adaptation are not simulated. The graph cursor advances through one complete cycle, then resets at the start of the next.</p><p>Descent follows the same spatial path in reverse. Generalized velocities reverse sign and time-reversed accelerations are preserved. The muscle force–velocity gain is recomputed and the force-sharing problem is solved again. Descent forces are not a reversed copy of ascent forces. Inverse-dynamics requirements are independently recomputed and checked.</p>''' if CYCLES else ''
model='''<h2>Required force, without an individual strength ceiling</h2><p>Prescribed motion and external load determine generalized force requirements. A 416-actuator MyoSim model and eight friction-limited foot supports satisfy those requirements. Total muscle tension is F_passive(length) + gain(length, velocity) × e, with e ≥ 0 and no hard upper bound. Native force–length–velocity and passive-stretch functions are retained. The allocation minimizes Σe² plus a small support-force cost. e is an optimization coefficient, not measured neural activation or firing rate. Generic muscle parameters affect force sharing, but do not define an individual's maximum lifting ability. <a href="https://mujoco.readthedocs.io/en/latest/modeling.html#muscles">MuJoCo muscle model</a>.</p>
<h2>Shoulder stability</h2><p>The reaction on the humerus is constrained to an outward-facing 20° glenoid cone using a conservative inscribed 16-face approximation. This directional constraint follows the approach discussed by <a href="https://journals.plos.org/plosone/article?id=10.1371/journal.pone.0295003">Belli et al. (2023)</a>; the complete published solver is not reproduced. The glenoid centre is estimated from a lateral scapular mesh patch, and the head centre uses the model's common GH rotation anchor. This is generic geometry, not subject-specific CT or a validated cartilage-contact model. Ligament/capsule material laws, translations and additional neural stabilization are not represented.</p>
<h2>Interpreting the latissimus</h2><p>The current solution assigns predominantly passive tension to the latissimus, with negligible active tension. This does not establish that the muscle is inactive in real pressing. Muscle length calibration and the allocation objective remain material limitations. No arbitrary latissimus force floor was added to match an expected recruitment pattern.</p>''' if PHYSIOLOGY else '<p>Legacy net-torque allocation draft; native active/passive physiology and GH stability are not included.</p>'
interval='One full 0–4.6 s cycle, including the two holds' if CYCLES else 'The 0–2 s ascent'
rack_text=''
if CYCLES:
 rack_text='''<h2>Rack placement and clearance</h2><p>The 28 mm shaft starts at clavicular height against the displayed upper-chest/clavicle surface. Calibration includes the shaft radius and a small mesh clearance. Both grips share the same start coordinates and horizontal path rule. A small forward/back arc and a fixed 25° head extension provide face clearance. The head pose is represented in both geometry and rigid-body dynamics.</p>
<p>Both feet use a shared 12 mm posterior placement relative to the initial reference stance, implemented through fixed hip and ankle angles. Leg angles remain fixed during the repetition. The force solution includes friction-limited foot support and zero root reserve forces. The generic elbow-flexion limit is extended from 130° to 150° to accommodate the rack; retained muscle parameters have not been separately validated over that added range.</p>
<p>Hand rendering uses one opaque skin surface per hand. The separate internal hand-bone display layer is omitted; wrist/hand bones and muscle actuators remain in the mechanical calculation. Actual rendered chest clearance, face clearance and the absence of a second visible hand-bone layer are checked before export. <a href="bar_geometry_validation.json">Rendered geometry checks</a>.</p>'''
correction='''<h2>Hip balance correction</h2><p>This revision balances 37 independent generalized coordinates, including left and right hip flexion. A previous substring filter incorrectly excluded hip_flexion when identifying finger ip_flexion. The trajectory is identical to the previous rack-corrected video. Recalculation corrects lower-body force sharing; the plotted major upper-body muscle forces are unchanged within numerical precision. <a href="hip_balance_correction.json">Before/after equilibrium checks</a>.</p>'''
balanced_hips=all(all('hip_flexion_'+side in json.loads((CASES[g]/'fullbody_metadata.json').read_text('utf-8'))['independent_coordinates'] for side in ['r','l']) for g in CASES)
if not balanced_hips:correction='<h2>Legacy lower-body limitation</h2><p>These older results omit hip-flexion equilibrium and should not be used for lower-body force interpretation. Regenerate with the corrected coordinate classification.</p>'
body='''<div class="eyebrow">EXERCISE MECHANICS / 01</div><h1>Overhead Press</h1><p class="lead">Standard Grip vs. Wide Grip</p><video src="ohp_grip_comparison_portrait.mp4" controls loop playsinline></video>
<h2>Controlled comparison</h2><p>180 cm / 90 kg male reference model, 100 kg bar, 65 cm standard grip versus 80 cm wide grip. Grip span is the only experimental input change. Start height, path rule, ascent duration, camera and visual scale are shared. Each grip reaches its own anatomical lockout height. These labels describe this comparison and are not universal definitions of standard and wide grip.</p>'''+correction+rack_text+cycle_text+model+'''
<h2>Reading the traces</h2><p>Solid: assisting or neutral tension relative to the required net moment of the selected coordinate. Dashed: opposing tension. Their sum is total group tension; the line style does not distinguish active from passive force. Shoulder groups use shoulder_elv; biceps and triceps use elbow_flexion. A muscle may have different roles at different joints. CSV exports include separate active and passive force components.</p>
<p>Muscle traces sum both sides. Joint reaction traces show the right side, including allocated muscle forces, segment weights, accelerations and bar loading. They represent model-transmitted resultant forces, not cartilage pressure, individual ligament force or injury risk.</p>
<h2>Mean / peak</h2><p>'''+interval+''' is the statistics interval. Means are time integrals divided by the interval duration. Replayed cycles, introductory freezes and the summary screen are excluded; values are not accumulated across three replays.</p>
<table><tr><th>Metric</th><th>Unit</th><th>Standard mean</th><th>Standard peak</th><th>Wide mean</th><th>Wide peak</th></tr>'''+''.join(rows)+'''</table>
<h2>Validation and limits</h2><p>Checks cover native muscle functions, active/passive force sums, equilibrium, independently computed shoulder reactions and GH force directions, hand positions, grip widths, common camera scale, repeated timeline alignment and the encoded video's 384 px bottom reserve. Global cubic B-spline IK reduces joint-path branch changes; force traces are not smoothed or clipped after solving. These are implementation checks, not experimental validation of recruitment or tissue loading. Absolute force values and grip differences remain model-dependent.</p>
<p><a href="grip_65_traces.csv">Standard grip time series</a> · <a href="grip_80_traces.csv">Wide grip time series</a> · <a href="grip_summary.csv">Summary CSV</a> · <a href="validation.json">Video checks</a> · <a href="physiology_checks.json">Physics checks</a> · <a href="CREDITS.txt">Asset credits and licences</a></p>'''
style='body{margin:32px auto;max-width:1000px;padding:0 24px;background:#0d1219;color:#d6e0e8;font:17px/1.8 "Segoe UI",sans-serif}h1{font-size:52px;margin:8px 0}h2{margin-top:40px;color:#d2dce5}.eyebrow{font-size:14px;letter-spacing:2px;color:#90a0ae}.lead{font-size:24px;color:#b9c7d2;margin-top:0}video{max-height:80vh;max-width:100%;display:block;margin:32px auto}a{color:#88c2cb}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:15px}td,th{padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #344452;text-align:right}td:first-child,th:first-child{text-align:left}'
(OUT/'grip_comparison_report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Overhead Press / Grip Comparison</title><style>'+style+'</style>'+body+'</html>',encoding='utf-8')
(OUT/'CREDITS.txt').write_text((ROOT/'assets/fullbody/CREDITS.md').read_text('utf-8'),encoding='utf-8')
if PHYSIOLOGY:
 checks={str(g):json.loads((CASES[g]/'physiology_independent_checks.json').read_text('utf-8')) for g in CASES}
 (OUT/'physiology_checks.json').write_text(json.dumps(checks,indent=2),encoding='utf-8')
print('GRIP_REPORT_PREPARED',flush=True)
